From ca5a24945bd3ddf95871a6cf11ed7481188685ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 10:48:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05485/11362] [outer-loop] adversarial_verify: normalize
 principle-wrapped fields before checking

Operator: 'Fix the linter to accept both forms.'

exp5161's earlier fix (previous commit) corrected ONE artifact's inference_substrate
from a {principle, value} dict to a bare string. A corpus-wide scan found 176
artifacts share that exact dict-wrapped structure for inference_substrate alone,
plus honest_verdict (9), duration_s (12), random_seed (14), and
reproducibility_checksum (14) -- every field several checks in this file read via a
bare d.get(...), all exposed to the same class of silent misbehavior (a verdict
that never matches its terminal-prefix regex, a duration check that silently
no-ops against the wrong floor, etc).

Fixing every individual read site is the whack-a-mole this bug already
demonstrates is unreliable -- the original exp5161 author wrote a {principle,
value} dict following an established, documented CLAUDE.md convention
('Principle-Annotated Artifact Fields'); it just didn't occur to anyone that
_inference_substrate_text() (str() on a dict produces a Python repr matching no
canonical value) wouldn't understand it.

Added _normalize_principle_wrapped_fields(): unwraps any top-level field shaped
{value: ..., principle: ...} to its bare value. Deliberately conservative --
requires BOTH keys present (not just 'value' alone, which could be real domain
data for some other field), and does not recurse into nested structures (only
top-level fields use this convention in practice). Wired into verify_artifact()
immediately after _flatten_metrics(), so every existing and future check
automatically sees the bare value with zero further per-check changes required.

10 new tests (unit tests for the normalizer's edge cases + end-to-end
reproduction of the exact exp5161 false-positive + a regression guard confirming
the fix does not weaken the check -- a genuinely-too-fast wrapped
live_llm_inference artifact must still be caught). Full existing suite (222
tests) still green, zero regressions. Corpus-wide dry-run sanity check
(--backfill --high-precision-only, 4564 artifacts scanned) found only 5
previously-unstamped qualifying artifacts -- no flood of new false positives.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
